  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Pages and navigation",
      "items": [
        "The hub lists every semester, subject and chapter. Its review board ranks started chapters by due date from each chapter's -checks and -log keys, and it draws the route line and radar from the same progress. (js/index.js:46–60, 93–112)",
        "Subjects with more than one course part get a Lecture / Exercise / Tutorial / Appendix switch: Lecture shows the chapter list, the other tabs list worked pages from their links in index.html. The open tab and each subject's fold are saved as hub-tabs and hub-folds. (js/index.js:142–145, 244–247; index.html:179–183)",
        "Guides, labs and worked pages share the contents rail. It fetches the hub's index.html, caches the chapter-and-exercise list in sessionStorage as nav-chapters-2, refetches when the cached list lacks the current page, and adds a Chapters fold and a Previous/Next pager of the same kind. (js/nav.js:220–227, 340–358)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Progress stays in the browser",
      "items": [
        "There is no server or account. Guides save ticks as <key>-checks and review days as <key>-log; labs save answers as <key>-lab and tick lab-<id> in the same -checks key, so the hub counts both. (js/guide.js:1–12; js/lab.js:1–9)",
        "Settings (theme, motion, text size) save as site-settings and apply from <head>; settings.js also loads the HUD layer, hud.js. Storage errors are swallowed, so nothing persists where storage is blocked. (js/settings.js:1–6, 23–26; js/hud.js:1–8)",
        "Lab experiments are per-chapter scripts that register with window.Lab; experiments with a generate() offer endless practice that is never saved. Their physics modules also load in node for the tests. (js/lab.js:103–104, 308–309, 560–570)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Authoring, data and publishing",
      "items": [
        "Page HTML is the single source: guide-to-tex.py writes the .tex and latexmk builds the PDF, both committed beside each guide, worked page and appendix; check-guide.py checks guides, labs, worked pages and appendices and fails when a .tex is stale. (tools/guide-to-tex.py:1334–1355; tools/check-guide.py:242–248, 101)",
        "The Graphify graph (graphify-out/graph.json) is refreshed by the workspace refresh script; graph-describe.py adds plain-English notes to graph.html and graph-orb.py lays the graph out in 3D as assets/graph-orb.json, which the hub's orb fetches when scrolled near. (tools/graph-orb.py:1–6, 27–28, 71; js/orb.js:1–5, 68)",
        "GitHub Pages publishes main from the root on every push; the Jekyll site CI workflow only builds the site as a check. Google Fonts serves Hanken Grotesk to every page's browser. (README.md:170–176; .github/workflows/jekyll-docker.yml:1–19; index.html:16–19)"
      ]
    }
  ]
}